cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the shipped measurement caches, please cite the manuscript below."
title: "Geometric Signatures of Scale in the XLS-R Family: Typological Alignment, Manifold Change, and Expert Separation in Self-Supervised Speech Models"
abstract: >-
  Measurement caches, figures and analysis code for a study of seven self-supervised speech encoders
  (XLSR-53, XLS-R-300M/1B/2B, MMS-300M/1B, mHuBERT-147) on 24 FLEURS languages plus the Rucheng dialect,
  with MLS as a second corpus. The paper reports a late alignment checkpoint at relative depth 0.75-0.79,
  a saturating step in intrinsic dimension between the 300M and 1B/2B tiers, disjoint tone and
  syllable-structure discriminant sets at Layer 38, and no ordering of recognition accuracy by any of the
  geometric quantities.
